                <pb facs="0121" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1021: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-09T23:00:00-06:00">December 9, 1937—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 10—9:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Referring to my telegram No. 34, December 9, 8 p.m., point number 9 should
                    read as follows: “A mutual offer of both Governments to solve the present
                    conflict by pacific means as established by international law. This offer does
                    not affect the Honduran reservation made to the general Treaty of Arbitration
                    signed January 5, 1929, in Washington, United States of America”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
